  },\n                \"links\": {\n                    \"self\": \"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/metagenomics/api/v1/annotations/interpro-identifiers/IPR002734?format=api\"\n                }\n                \"type\": \"interpro-identifiers\",\n                \"id\": \"IPR007428\",\n                \"attributes\": {\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nMGnify API: archiving, analysis and integration of metagenomics data. EMBL-EBI (https://www.ebi.ac.uk/metagenomics/api/v1/analyses/MGYA00128632/interpro-identifiers?format=api)\nciteturn8search3 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today;             \"first\": \"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/metagenomics/api/v1/analyses/MGYA00128632/interpro-identifiers? ...             \"last\": \"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/metagenomics/api/v1/analyses/MGYA00128632/interpro-identifiers? ...                     \"description\": \"Ammonium/urea transporter\"\n                    \"description\": \"Sodium:alanine symporter\"\n                },\n                \"links\": {\n                    \"self\": \"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/metagenomics/api/v1/annotations/interpro-identifiers/IPR001463?format=api\"\n                }\n            },\n            {\n                \"type\": \"interpro-identifiers\",\n                \"id\": \"IPR005135\",\n                \"attributes\": {\n                    \"accession\": \"IPR005135\",\n                    \"count\": 4643,\n                    \"description\": \"Endonuclease/exonuclease/phosphatase\"\n                },\n                \"links\": {\n                    \"self\": \"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/metagenomics/api/v1/annotations/interpro-identifiers/IPR005135?format=api\"\n                }\n            },\n            {\n                \"type\": \"interpro-identifiers\",\n                \"id\": \"IPR013766\",\n                \"attributes\": {\n                    \"accession\": \"IPR013766\",\n                    \"count\": 4639,\n                    \"description\": \"Thioredoxin domain\"\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n___________________________                                                                ________________________ (https://www.ccap.ac.uk/wp-content/uploads/MR_SP.pdf)\nciteturn8view0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 days ago; Content type: application/pdf; Number of pages: 1; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://www.ccap.ac.uk/wp-content/uploads/MR_SP.pdf\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 48\nL0@P0: SP (Spirulina Medium)\nL1@P0: Some marine cyanobacteria\nL2@P0: Stocks per litre\nL3@P0: (1) Micronutrient solution\nL4@P0: ZnSO4.7H2O 0.001 g\nL5@P0:  MnSO4.7H2O 0.002 g\nL6@P0:  H3BO3 0.010 g\nL7@P0:  Na2MoO4.2H2O 0.001 g\nL8@P0:  Co(NO3)2.6H2O 0.001 g\nL9@P0:  CuSO4.5H2O 0.00005 g\nL10@P0:  FeSO4.7H2O 0.70 g\nL11@P0:  EDTANa2 0.80 g\nL12@P0:  May be stored frozen at –20o C.\nL13@P0:  (2) Vitamin solution\nL14@P0:  Biotin 0.0002 g\nL15@P0:  Calcium pantothenate 0.02 g\nL16@P0:  Cyanocobalamin 0.004 g\nL17@P0:  Folic acid 0.0004 g\nL18@P0:  Inositol 1.00 g\nL19@P0:  Nicotinic acid 0.02 g\nL20@P0:  Thiamine HCl 0.10 g\nL21@P0:  Thymine 0.60 g\nL22@P0:  May be stored frozen at -20 C.\nL23@P0: Medium\nL24@P0: This medium is made up in 2 parts to reduce precipitation when autoclaving. For\nL25@P0: each part add the components to around 900 mls deionised water and then top up\nL26@P0: to 1 litre with deionised water.\nL27@P0: Part 1 per litre\nL28@P0: NaHCO3 27.22 g\nL29@P0: Na2CO3 8.06 g\nL30@P0: K2HPO4 1.00 g\nL31@P0:  Part 2 per litre\nL32@P0: NaNO3 5.00 g\nL33@P0: K2SO4 2.00 g\nL34@P0: NaCl 2.00 g\nL35@P0: MgSO4.7H2O 0.40 g\nL36@P0: CaCl2.2H2O 0.02 g\nL37@P0: FeSO4.7H2O 0.02 g\nL38@P0: EDTANa2 0.16 g\nL39@P0: Micronutrient solution (1) 10.0 ml\nL40@P0: Vitamin solution (2) 5.00 ml\nL41@P0: per litre final medium\nL42@P0: Part 1 500.0 ml\nL43@P0: Part 2 500.0 ml\nL44@P0: media recipes\nL45@P0: Autoclave parts 1 and 2 separately at 15 psi, allow to cool then mix 1:1 aseptically.\nL46@P0: CCAP (Culture Collection of Algae and Protozoa), Scottish Marine Institute, Oban, Argyll, PA37 1QA, UK\nL47@P0: Tel: +44 (0)1631 559000 Fax: +44 (0)1631 559001 Email: ccap@sams.ac.uk Web: www.ccap.ac.uk\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n___________________________                                                                ________________________ (https://www.ccap.ac.uk/wp-content/uploads/MR_PC.pdf)\nciteturn8view1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 months ago; Content type: application/pdf; Number of pages: 1; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://www.ccap.ac.uk/wp-content/uploads/MR_PC.pdf\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 34\nL0@P0: QF 09\nL1@P0: Media Preparation Recipe Template\nL2@P0: Revision: 002\nL3@P0: Approved: 29 MAY 26\nL4@P0: Created on:\nL5@P0: 29 May 2026\nL6@P0: CCAP (Culture Collection of Algae and Protozoa), SAMS Ltd,\nL7@P0: Scottish Association for Marine Science, Oban, Argyll, PA37 1QA\nL8@P0: Tel: +44 (0)1631 559000 Email: ccap@sams.ac.uk\nL9@P0: Web: www.ccap.ac.uk\nL10@P0: Page 1 of 1\nL11@P0: PC (Prescott's & Carrier's Solution)\nL12@P0: Freshwater protozoa\nL13@P0: Stocks per litre\nL14@P0: (1) MgSO4.7H2O 2.0 g\nL15@P0: KCl 5.0 g\nL16@P0: CaCl2 10.0 g\nL17@P0: NaCl 10.0 g\nL18@P0: Autoclave at 15 psi for 15 minutes. Dispense any excess stocks into 1 ml aliquots and freeze.\nL19@P0: (2) CaHPO4 0.36 g\nL20@P0: Autoclave at 15 psi for 15 minutes. Dispense any excess stocks into 10 ml aliquots and\nL21@P0: freeze.\nL22@P0: Medium per litre\nL23@P0: Stock solution 1 1 ml\nL24@P0: Stock solution 2 10 ml\nL25@P0: Using aseptic technique, make up to 1 litre with sterile deionised water. It may be necessary\nL26@P0: to decant supernatant from precipitate in final medium.\nL27@P0: Alternatively, after autoclaving, it might be necessary to filter through 0.2-micron filter to\nL28@P0: remove precipitates.\nL29@P0: Reference\nL30@P0: Prescott, D. M., & Carrier, R. F. (1964). Experimental procedures and cultural methods for\nL31@P0: Euplotes eurystomus and Amoeba proteus. In Methods in cell biology (Vol. 1, pp. 85-95).\nL32@P0: Academic Press. – adapted for CCAP\nL33@P0: Reviewed: 30th June 2026\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nMedium data (https://www.jcm.riken.jp/cgi-bin/jcm/jcm_grmd?GRMD=574)\nciteturn8view2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://www.jcm.riken.jp/cgi-bin/jcm/jcm_grmd?GRMD=574\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 50\nL0: # Medium data\nL1: \nL2: Search for medium no. = [574].\nL3: \nL4: * * *\nL5: \nL6: Unless otherwise stated, sterilize media by autoclaving at 121°C for 15 min.\nL7: \nL8: * * *\nL9: \nL10: 574   DB CHARACTERIZATION MEDIUM NO. 2\nL11: MDS salt water (see below)  | ` 833.0    `  | ml\nL12: FeCl_{2} solution (see Medium No. 【0†187】)  | ` 1.0    `  | ml\nL13: Trace element solution (see Medium No. 【0†187】)  | ` 1.0    `  | ml\nL14: Peptone (Oxoid)  | ` 0.25   `  | g\nL15: Yeast extract (BD-Difco)  | ` 0.05   `  | g\nL16: Add components and bring volume to 980 ml with distilled water. For preparation of solid medium, add 20 g/L agar (if necessary, use washed agar as described below). Autoclave, and after cooling, add the following solutions (filter-sterilized or *autoclaved) to the medium:\nL17: 1 M NH_{4}Cl  | ` 5.0    `  | ml\nL18: Potassium phosphate buffer* (see below)  | ` 2.0    `  | ml\nL19: Vitamin solution (see below)  | ` 3.0    `  | ml\nL20: 1 M Sodium pyruvate solution  | ` 10.0    `  | ml\nL21: Readjust pH to 7.0 - 7.5 with a sterilized 10% Na_{2}CO_{3} solution, if necessary.\nL22: Washed agar:\nL23: Stir agar in distilled water and stand still for 30 min. Then, remove supernatant by decantation. Repeat the washing at least twice.\nL24: MDS salt water:\nL25: NaCl  | ` 240.0    `  | g\nL26: MgCl_{2}·6H_{2}O  | ` 30.0    `  | g\nL27: MgSO_{4}·7H_{2}O  | ` 35.0    `  | g\nL28: KCl  | ` 7.0    `  | g\nL29: 1 M CaCl_{2} solution  | ` 5.0    `  | ml\nL30: Add components to distilled water and bring volume to 1.0 L. Adjust pH to 7.5 with 1 M Tris base.\nL31: Potassium phosphate buffer:\nL32: 1 M K_{2}HPO_{4}  | ` 83.4    `  | ml\nL33: 1 M KH_{2}PO_{4}  | ` 16.6    `  | ml\nL34: Combine the two solutions and check that pH is close to 7.5. Add an equal volume of distilled water.\nL35: Vitamin solution:\nL36: Biotin  | ` 3.0    `  | mg\nL37: Folic acid  | ` 4.0    `  | mg\nL38: Pyridoxine·HCl  | ` 50.0    `  | mg\nL39: Thiamine·HCl  | ` 33.0    `  | mg\nL40: Riboflavin  | ` 10.0    `  | mg\nL41: Nicotinic acid  | ` 33.0    `  | mg\nL42: DL-Calcium pantothenate  | ` 17.0    `  | mg\nL43: Vitamin B_{1}_{2}  | ` 17.0    `  | mg\nL44: p-Aminobenzoic acid  | ` 13.0    `  | mg\nL45: Lipoic acid  | ` 10.0    `  | mg\nL46: Distilled water  | ` 1.0    `  | L\nL47: * * *\nL48: \nL49: Copyright © 2026 Microbe Division (JCM) - All Rights Reserved\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nMedium data (https://www.jcm.riken.jp/cgi-bin/jcm/jcm_grmd?GRMD=941)\nciteturn8view3 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 3 months ago; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://www.jcm.riken.jp/cgi-bin/jcm/jcm_grmd?GRMD=941\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 35\nL0: # Medium data\nL1: \nL2: Search for medium no. = [941].\nL3: \nL4: * * *\nL5: \nL6: Unless otherwise stated, sterilize media by autoclaving at 121°C for 15 min.\nL7: \nL8: * * *\nL9: \nL10: 941   SULFURIMONAS HONGKONGENSIS MEDIUM\nL11: Solution A:\nL12: KH_{2}PO_{4} ` 2.0    ` g\nL13: KNO_{3} ` 2.0    ` g\nL14: NH_{4}Cl ` 1.0    ` g\nL15: NaCl ` 25.0    ` g\nL16: SL-4 trace element solution (see Medium No. 【0†340】) ` 2.0    ` ml\nL17: Distilled water ` 930.0    ` ml\nL18: Adjust pH to 7.0 with NaOH.\nL19: Solution B:\nL20: MgCl_{2}·6H_{2}O ` 0.8    ` g\nL21: Distilled water ` 10.0    ` ml\nL22: Solution C:\nL23: Na_{2}S_{2}O_{4}·2H_{2}O ` 5.0    ` g\nL24: Distilled water ` 40.0    ` ml\nL25: Solution D:\nL26: NaHCO_{3} ` 1.0    ` g\nL27: Distilled water ` 20.0    ` ml\nL28: Solution E:\nL29: FeSO_{4}·7H_{2}O ` 0.2    ` mg\nL30: 0.1 N H_{2}SO_{4} solution ` 1.0    ` ml\nL31: Separately autoclave Solutions A, B, C and E under a N_{2} atmosphere. Filter-sterilize Solution D. After sterilization, combine all solutions and store under a N_{2} atmosphere.\nL32: * * *\nL33: \nL34: Copyright © 2026 Microbe Division (JCM) - All Rights Reserved\n"
